{
  "id": "ecochg",
  "term": "ECochG",
  "definition": "ECochG, or electrocochleography, is a test that records the electrical activity produced by the inner ear and auditory nerve in response to brief sounds using electrodes placed on or near the ear. It has been used to help assess inner-ear disorders and is also used during cochlear implant surgery to monitor cochlear function in real time.",
